Additionally, this is an "above-the-line" deduction (meaning you don't have to itemize to take it), but it is subject to income limits. For 2023, the deduction phases out for single filers with a Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) between $75,000 and $90,000. 
Because your total gross income is roughly $94,915 ($84,900 W-2 + $8,900 consulting + $1,115 interest/dividends), **you are completely phased out and will not be able to deduct your student loan interest.**

