*   **Form 8829:** Required if you choose the "Actual Expenses" method for your home office.
*   **Schedule SE:** To calculate self-employment tax on your net freelance profit.
*   *(Note on Interest/Dividends):* Your $920 from Marcus and $480 from Fidelity total $1,400. Because this is under the $1,500 threshold, you likely won't need Schedule B, but you will still report the totals directly on the designated lines of your Form 1040.

